sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor T0 as Tutor (web UI)
    actor D as Admin (web UI)
    actor S as Student (web UI)
    participant G as API Gateway (Traefik)
    participant T as Tutor
    participant B as Booking
    participant R as Review
    participant Q as RabbitMQ
    participant N as Notification

    Note over T0,N: REST = solid arrow, gRPC = labelled "gRPC", event = labelled "AMQP", local DB step = note box
    Note over T0,N: Every protected REST call passes gateway forward-auth to Auth and reaches the owner with an actor assertion (UC-03 steps 5 to 7)

    rect rgb(255, 236, 236)
    Note over T0,T: Phase 1 · Listing or document change goes to admin review
    T0->>G: REST POST /api/profiles/me/tutor/drafts, PUT drafts/{id}, then POST drafts/{id}/submit (TUTOR capability, If-Match)
    G->>T: REST request + actor assertion
    Note over T: Local DB transaction (MongoDB tutor_db): draft kind REVISION becomes PENDING,<br/>outbox row tutor.submission-submitted. The approved public version stays visible
    T-->>T0: 200 submission PENDING
    D->>G: REST POST /api/admin/tutor-requests/{id}/review (ADMIN, APPROVE, If-Match)
    G->>T: REST request + actor assertion
    Note over T: One local transaction: revision APPROVED and becomes the public content.<br/>No Auth grant needed, the tutor is already ACTIVE
    T-->>D: 200 approved
    end

    rect rgb(255, 244, 230)
    Note over T0,T: Phase 2 · Tutor publishes the listing and adds subjects
    T0->>G: REST PATCH /api/profiles/me/tutor/publication (published true, If-Match, Idempotency-Key)
    G->>T: REST request + actor assertion
    T-->>T0: 200 workspace, published
    T0->>G: REST POST /api/profiles/me/tutor/subjects (name, description, hourlyRate, format, learningAreas)
    G->>T: REST request + actor assertion
    alt Active tutor and valid input
        Note over T: Local DB transaction: subject saved under the tutor (max 100)
        T-->>T0: 201 subject
    else Not activated, unknown learning area or blank text
        T-->>T0: 403 TUTOR_NOT_ACTIVE or 422 VALIDATION_FAILED
    end
    end

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
    Note over T0,B: Phase 3 · Tutor opens dated 30-minute slots (owned by Booking)
    T0->>G: REST PUT /api/profiles/me/tutor/availability/{date}/{time} (state OPEN, subjectIds, If-None-Match: * to create or If-Match to edit)
    G->>B: REST request + actor assertion
    B->>T: gRPC GetTutorEligibility (approved, activated?)
    T-->>B: tutorId, approved, activated
    B->>T: gRPC GetBookableSubject for each subjectId (must be the caller's own)
    T-->>B: subject snapshot
    alt Slot free or open
        Note over B: Local DB transaction (PostgreSQL booking_db):<br/>lock row, insert or update slot OPEN, replace slot_subjects
        B-->>T0: 200 slot, ETag = revision
    else Slot already HELD or BOOKED
        B-->>T0: 409 SLOT_LOCKED (a paid booking keeps its slot)
    else Stale revision, or subject not owned
        B-->>T0: 412 REVISION_MISMATCH or 422 SUBJECT_NOT_OWNED
    end
    end

    rect rgb(243, 235, 255)
    Note over S,N: Phase 4 · Students can now discover the listing, and the tutor is notified
    S->>G: REST GET /api/discovery/tutors (public route, no token)
    G->>T: REST request
    T->>R: gRPC GetRatingSummaries (batch)
    R-->>T: rating summaries
    T->>B: gRPC BatchGetAvailability (next open slot, free count)
    B-->>T: availability summaries
    T-->>S: 200 ranked list of published subjects with ratings and availability
    T-)Q: AMQP publish tutor.submission-decided (outbox worker, after commit)
    Q-)N: AMQP deliver event
    Note over N: Dedupe event, create jobs for the tutor (simulated delivery)
    end
